. The offset just appears without touching it.\n\nI see you have 2 monitors, I can use the `Spacedesk` software to simulate a screen with my tablet, and this situation is 100% reproduced when starting and closing the software in maximized godot editor window.\nTherefore, I believe these issues all refer to the same problem.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5411332261/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5411362241","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105745#issuecomment-5411362241","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105745","id":5411362241,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQorVwQ","user":{"login":"Zireael07","id":4525388,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MjUzODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4525388?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07","html_url":"https://github.com/Zireael07","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zireael07/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T13:49:28Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T13:49:28Z","body":"@saierXP I recall a second issue where the problem is also reproduced in Spacedesk. Are you sure it's not an issue with Spacedesk itself?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5411362241/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5412213319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105745#issuecomment-5412213319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105745","id":5412213319,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQpfSRw","user":{"login":"saierXP","id":45038185,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDM4MTg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45038185?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP","html_url":"https://github.com/saierXP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saierXP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T14:50:48Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T15:56:35Z","body":"> I recall a second issue where the problem is also reproduced in Spacedesk. Are you sure it's not an issue with Spacedesk itself?\n\nMaybe you are right, I used a laptop with a second physical monitor, and turning the monitor off and on repeatedly did not reproduce the problem.\n\n**Edit: Laptop with spacedesk doesn't cause screen shift; it's probably because my laptop's graphics card is too old.**\n\n**Edit2: \nChanging the screen refresh rate in Windows settings can also trigger this issue. This will make the screen going black and then back to normal, similar to Spacedesk simulating a table connected as an extended screen.\nChanging resolution and scale can't make screen offset.**\n\nAdditionally, my laptop doesn't have screen shift when changing window sizes, but my desktop computer does.\n\nKeeping editor in the background can also cause this issue, I aslo have encountered it many times. \n\nThen it seems to duplicate with this issue.\n- #94838\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5412213319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]